# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/100 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 18 deg Earth-central angle (2141 km away, zenith 113.2 deg,
# azimuth 0 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 1.1e+06 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.375 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw -58.89 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source E_DISTPAR0024
E_DISTPAR0024.ParticleType 1
E_DISTPAR0024.Beam FarFieldGaussian 91.271 301.110 4.014
E_DISTPAR0024.Spectrum File E_DISTPAR0024_spectrum.dat
E_DISTPAR0024.Flux 0.103773
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835634345.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): E_DISTPAR0024_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
E_DISTPAR0024.Lightcurve File false E_DISTPAR0024_lightcurve_shifted.dat
E_DISTPAR0024.EarthOccultation false
